<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mi'kmaq</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Micmac</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mi'kmaq are an Indigenous people of the Atlantic region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>, living in what are now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-edward-island">Prince Edward Island</a>, New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaspe-peninsula">Gaspé Peninsula</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a>. They speak an Algonquian language and were members of the Wabanaki Confederacy. Close allies of the French in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acadia">Acadia</a>, they fought the British in a series of wars before making treaties of peace and friendship in the 18th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mikmaq.jpg" alt="Mi'kmaq" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rev. Father Pacifique Buisson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mikmaq_State_Flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
